From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
d3drm: frame state, reference frames and Move

Frames keep colour, material/sort/z-buffer modes, scene fog and background
state, axes and boxes, and implement positions, orientations, velocities and
rotations in the space of a reference frame, Move with its pre- and
post-order callbacks over the whole tree, Transform/InverseTransform and the
vector variants, and LookAt, for IDirect3DRMFrame, 2 and 3.
